# B&B optimization example for register-symmetry.
# A ten-vertex clique needs ten distinct colors. With nine registers and
# forbidden spills, canonical register naming avoids exploring permutations of
# equivalent assignments.
# Run from the repository root.
# Enabled:  ./build-clang-modules/pbqp --solve=bnb -Werror -O0 --numthreads=1 --timeout=0.7 -fregister-symmetry examples/pbqp/individual/bnb-register-symmetry.pbqp
# Baseline: ./build-clang-modules/pbqp --solve=bnb -Werror -O0 --numthreads=1 --timeout=0.7 -fno-register-symmetry examples/pbqp/individual/bnb-register-symmetry.pbqp
# Observed with Clang 21 Release on Intel Core Ultra X7 358H.
# Median elapsed CLI time over five alternating runs, including startup.
# Enabled: 4.4 ms, 5/5 infeasible.
# Baseline: 704.6 ms, 1/5 infeasible, 4/5 timeout.

PBQP 2
NODES 10
EDGES 45
MATRICES 1
NODE 0 10 INF 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
NODE 1 10 INF 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
NODE 2 10 INF 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
